      "raw": "I'm very bad about that arguments thing, because my quasi-autistic brain doesn't comprehend why saying \"please calm down\" doesn't work at all.\n\nThe broad discussion of Vanessa's solo investigations makes me think a LOT of the rare solo Martian Manhunter (my favorite superhero outside Sentinels ever) books, where he's mostly John Jones the detective, occasionally using his incredibly strong powers to overcome minor obstacles to the case he's solving.\n\n\"The fact that there is a Vanessa Long that has powers is a fixed point, but the way you get there is quite messy.\" All I can think of is JGL's character at the end of The Dark Knight Rises being like \"call me Robin\" when he had literally nothing in common with Robin the whole movie.  They could called him Azrael or Damien or the kid's name from Batman Beyond, it'd be at least as good in all those cases.  (I also like to think that Rule 63 Visionary is a guy named Van Essa-Long, because I  that universe, snooty aristocrat males hyphenate their names and his mother was an Essa, from the West Exhamshire Essas.)\n\nDark Visionary would do a Count Barzakh on Muse if she got the chance.\n\nIt took until the letter in this episode for me to think of a take in the Arcane Freedom Five episode.  I want to see the Freedom Five Promo versions of those heroes, where they get new high magic costumes from whoever takes the Luminary role in that universe, who is probably not Delta-V Blade.  I'm thinking maybe it's a villainous Naturalist who's allied to Akash'Thribhut and Bugbear and Quetzalcoatl. \n\nI like that a person who's racist against spiders is just an Arachnophobe.  Hopefully Charlotte's presidential run can count on Adam's vote in 2028.\n\nVisionary or maybe Eclipse lesbian lover confirmed: former Bollywood sensation Saari Natsaari.\n\nIf you listen to this episode, make sure not to miss the post-credits scene!  I can't believe it took them this long to do Who's On First, but it was so good, well worth the wait, I wish they'd done more of it.\n\n[quote=\"Trajector, post:13, topic:19893, full:true\"]\nIt's probably my single favorite post on this entire forum, hehe!\n[/quote]\n\nAwww, that link is dead now, I'm sorry your favorite post is gone....\n\n[quote=\"Powerhound_2000, post:1, topic:19893\"]\nLets hope it's not all in her mind.\n[/quote]\n\nI really wish it had been!  A psionic character whose entire supporting cast are imaginary friends would be so cool.  I'm definitely making that for like the Final Wasteland or something.",
